1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,581
Snakes were killing my people.

2
00:00:02,261 --> 00:00:03,081
God's cure?

3
00:00:03,681 --> 00:00:04,222
A snake.

4
00:00:05,082 --> 00:00:05,862
I am Moses.

5
00:00:06,703 --> 00:00:08,283
My people spoke against God.

6
00:00:08,863 --> 00:00:09,724
He sent snakes.

7
00:00:10,404 --> 00:00:11,044
Many died.

8
00:00:11,544 --> 00:00:13,245
They cried, We have sinned.

9
00:00:13,965 --> 00:00:14,525
I prayed.

10
00:00:15,246 --> 00:00:17,086
God did not take the snakes away.

11
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:20,508
He said: make a snake, set it on a pole.

12
00:00:21,068 --> 00:00:23,029
I made one of brass, and lifted it up.

13
00:00:23,589 --> 00:00:25,710
Anyone bitten who looked at it, lived.

14
00:00:27,911 --> 00:00:29,691
The cure looked like the thing that was killing

15
00:00:29,731 --> 00:00:30,031
them.

16
00:00:30,532 --> 00:00:32,712
I lived long before Jesus, God's Son.

17
00:00:33,413 --> 00:00:37,174
But He said: as Moses lifted up the serpent

18
00:00:37,214 --> 00:00:39,635
in the wilderness, even so must the Son of

19
00:00:39,695 --> 00:00:43,636
man be lifted up Lifted up: He meant Himself,

20
00:00:43,817 --> 00:00:44,297
on a cross.

21
00:00:44,797 --> 00:00:46,738
A later writer, Paul, said that on the cross

22
00:00:46,798 --> 00:00:48,538
God made him to be sin for us.

23
00:00:50,619 --> 00:00:52,820
The bitten looked at a snake, and lived.

24
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,241
Believe in Jesus, lifted up on the cross, and

25
00:00:56,301 --> 00:00:56,601
live.
